{
    "word": "afloat",
    "lang_code": "en",
    "source_file_to_entries": {
        "raw-wiktextract-data.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "7c96094e-7ac7-3e64-9373-282ee75e7b89",
                "word": "afloat",
                "pos": "adj",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "72da0118-b03c-3c72-bc8a-ddc8c83d7a1d",
                        "entry_id": "7c96094e-7ac7-3e64-9373-282ee75e7b89",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Floating."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "not-comparable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "101e2c9c-2800-463f-9b30-36e1d7b41c1a",
                                "sense_id": "72da0118-b03c-3c72-bc8a-ddc8c83d7a1d",
                                "text": "A rubber duck and other toys were afloat in the bath."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "3ce1e4ed-d213-4a52-a294-a722f1625518",
                                "sense_id": "72da0118-b03c-3c72-bc8a-ddc8c83d7a1d",
                                "text": "On such a full sea are we now afloat; / And we must take the current when it serves, / Or lose our ventures."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "b319fe95-dc29-3fdf-9203-82aba570a0b4",
                        "entry_id": "7c96094e-7ac7-3e64-9373-282ee75e7b89",
                        "glosses": [
                            "In, or found while in, a vessel at sea or on another body of water."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "not-comparable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "c06fc5e6-0f58-4a20-b7d8-687a903fbed2",
                                "sense_id": "b319fe95-dc29-3fdf-9203-82aba570a0b4",
                                "text": "[…] that trade […] may likewise employ many useful hands both ashore and afloat,"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "640214c9-0061-32bf-b949-ec1a87a3d2d5",
                        "entry_id": "7c96094e-7ac7-3e64-9373-282ee75e7b89",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Floating in the air; flowing freely; not tied, braided, etc. (of hair or clothing)"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "not-comparable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "55394796-6a4b-40cf-a396-2cfaf204d3d0",
                                "sense_id": "640214c9-0061-32bf-b949-ec1a87a3d2d5",
                                "text": "her black hair loose and a-float down her dazzling white neck",
                                "translation": "Fanny Hill",
                                "english": "Fanny Hill"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "79485a44-0878-4a87-9e6f-ec067b28bd30",
                                "sense_id": "640214c9-0061-32bf-b949-ec1a87a3d2d5",
                                "text": "unbound silvery-gold tresses afloat beneath a jeweled coronet"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b95b81e4-9ef6-4d72-a290-865dd693a1cd",
                                "sense_id": "640214c9-0061-32bf-b949-ec1a87a3d2d5",
                                "text": "[…] she roars down the street, dreads and feathers and cape afloat,"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "14484592-2905-30ce-bce6-377da782135d",
                        "entry_id": "7c96094e-7ac7-3e64-9373-282ee75e7b89",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Covered with water, bearing floating objects."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "not-comparable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "535d3f42-1297-4e96-a48d-c13891df782f",
                                "sense_id": "14484592-2905-30ce-bce6-377da782135d",
                                "text": "The decks are afloat."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "7e1c6ac3-8bd6-4c42-bea5-d531dcbcf663",
                                "sense_id": "14484592-2905-30ce-bce6-377da782135d",
                                "text": "The yard was afloat. Jody looked out of the window and saw two drowned biddies floating about with upturned bellies."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "e2fb6b78-8730-394b-a978-7a9c14a1a956",
                        "entry_id": "7c96094e-7ac7-3e64-9373-282ee75e7b89",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Covered, overspread, filled (with or in something)."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "figuratively",
                            "not-comparable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "afc1f7da-80d8-4a8d-84ef-21f6b0fd7a95",
                                "sense_id": "e2fb6b78-8730-394b-a978-7a9c14a1a956",
                                "text": "The larch-wood was afloat with clear, lyric green,"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ea9be0f8-8a42-4442-9aa6-a449a2e1e62c",
                                "sense_id": "e2fb6b78-8730-394b-a978-7a9c14a1a956",
                                "text": "The world was afloat in primrose light, pale and exquisite."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a1b98b6d-1062-4fb3-8044-357d837e412c",
                                "sense_id": "e2fb6b78-8730-394b-a978-7a9c14a1a956",
                                "text": "The lobby was afloat with men, single and married, meeting pretty women in bright dresses and pants suits, single and married."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "eb00dccd-2681-3c66-9837-15e16eb6c068",
                        "entry_id": "7c96094e-7ac7-3e64-9373-282ee75e7b89",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Having just enough resources to continue to operate; barely able to pay expenses; (of a private individual, family, etc.) keeping one's head above water."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "not-comparable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "6ea0ebb2-c6b5-41dc-8566-3bb3c2174616",
                                "sense_id": "eb00dccd-2681-3c66-9837-15e16eb6c068",
                                "text": "The donation will keep our business afloat for quite a while."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d342b852-dc8a-4ad4-9de6-2c1380565c01",
                                "sense_id": "eb00dccd-2681-3c66-9837-15e16eb6c068",
                                "text": "[…] you nede not to be sorye, as thoughe your frendely liberalitie had not be very acceptable vnto me. I haue receaued euery thing, and now I am afloate, by your lyberall sendyng."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "7f2d55af-1c15-445e-bc5c-d8e69c46bd00",
                                "sense_id": "eb00dccd-2681-3c66-9837-15e16eb6c068",
                                "text": "He […] endeavoured, by forcing himself into a lower path of life than any he had hitherto trod, to keep himself afloat, with the portion of some tradesman’s daughter, whom he meant to espouse."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "4bba473b-ee89-4ad6-b923-be001a01fe6f",
                                "sense_id": "eb00dccd-2681-3c66-9837-15e16eb6c068",
                                "text": "[…] the price poor Jos Osborne had paid for her two horses was in itself sufficient to keep their little establishment afloat for a year, at least;"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "3bf255e0-e4f4-496f-9074-57e52e707e7b",
                                "sense_id": "eb00dccd-2681-3c66-9837-15e16eb6c068",
                                "text": "They somehow manage to keep \"afloat,\" so as to obtain the needful funds to pay their passages and to purchase, tools and rations."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c0a5d081-32a9-4a56-a897-a1175109ebc8",
                                "sense_id": "eb00dccd-2681-3c66-9837-15e16eb6c068",
                                "text": "The clan handouts that kept other Somalis afloat were absent here, as the Yibros were so few and so poor."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "928659d7-f239-4d7b-8925-1944aebed4bb",
                                "sense_id": "eb00dccd-2681-3c66-9837-15e16eb6c068",
                                "text": "The party’s cash crunch is serious enough that party officials have weighed seeking a line of credit to help it stay afloat, a development first reported by The New York Times."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "2e5402ac-4281-3d3d-b8b1-5d54bfb6ccd3",
                        "entry_id": "7c96094e-7ac7-3e64-9373-282ee75e7b89",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Believed or talked about by many people; being passed from person to person."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "figuratively",
                            "not-comparable",
                            "usually"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "758e994c-56ba-41cd-91b6-a0c51a7ae3a9",
                                "sense_id": "2e5402ac-4281-3d3d-b8b1-5d54bfb6ccd3",
                                "text": "The supervisor was never fired, though countless accusations of dishonesty were afloat."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f77d117f-f64c-4e9d-9a0b-439633df670e",
                                "sense_id": "2e5402ac-4281-3d3d-b8b1-5d54bfb6ccd3",
                                "text": "[…] she and I were accepted, whatever ugly rumours had been afloat in the past year, as man and wife."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "d8a13d61-c04e-372c-9ba7-c0deec85c810",
                        "entry_id": "7c96094e-7ac7-3e64-9373-282ee75e7b89",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Stimulated, aroused, activated."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "figuratively",
                            "not-comparable",
                            "obsolete"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "d11dc6dd-8d18-4681-8597-01093b4e10b8",
                                "sense_id": "d8a13d61-c04e-372c-9ba7-c0deec85c810",
                                "text": "You’ll find, when once my passion is afloat, / The soul of Caesar, in a petticoat!"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "827eae70-88f0-45fe-acde-ddf33957f165",
                                "sense_id": "d8a13d61-c04e-372c-9ba7-c0deec85c810",
                                "text": "My half frozen blood and my fears again afloat made me tremble through every limb;"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "49f869c5-cac2-3297-b98c-ddf4094c61a2",
                        "entry_id": "7c96094e-7ac7-3e64-9373-282ee75e7b89",
                        "glosses": [
                            "In a state of confusion, bewilderment, or distraction."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "figuratively",
                            "not-comparable",
                            "obsolete"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "73320648-895f-4e66-8f5d-056051b7678e",
                                "sense_id": "49f869c5-cac2-3297-b98c-ddf4094c61a2",
                                "text": "1789, Edward Gibbon, letter to Lord Sheffield dated August 1789, in Miscellaneous Works, London: A. Strahan et al., 1796, p. 201,\nI know not what to say; my mind is all afloat; yet you will not reproach me with caprice or inconstancy."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6625730e-8b8d-4f40-ad78-8f97b5e90b68",
                                "sense_id": "49f869c5-cac2-3297-b98c-ddf4094c61a2",
                                "text": "[…] he could correctly analyze and parse any sentence you could give him, no matter how complex; but when it came to talking he was all afloat."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "e0674a4e-42bf-4ec9-bc44-a3b9e8f285ea",
                        "source_entry_id": "7c96094e-7ac7-3e64-9373-282ee75e7b89",
                        "source_sense_description": "floating",
                        "target_lang_word": "à flot",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "à flot",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7fb707fc-911d-3e75-8121-794955b713dc",
                                        "entry_id": "59a9f3ea-b16d-3c44-a4a8-526b8ff66717",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "En train de flotter."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "literally"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8f6cdf9d-93fe-30e1-8263-437b6f7482dc",
                                        "entry_id": "59a9f3ea-b16d-3c44-a4a8-526b8ff66717",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Avoir suffisamment d'argent pour vivre."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "figuratively"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "26f90ca6-3c63-4593-94e1-85265922a438",
                                                "sense_id": "8f6cdf9d-93fe-30e1-8263-437b6f7482dc",
                                                "text": "Être à flot, se remettre à flot, se maintenir à flot."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "be796f0f-25a6-44cc-bc21-e6f7ec127229",
                                                "sense_id": "8f6cdf9d-93fe-30e1-8263-437b6f7482dc",
                                                "text": "Mais ces individus veulent qu’il soit utilisé comme ils l’ont prévu. Pour permettre aux personnes en situation de précarité de simplement se maintenir à flot et de rendre leurs enfants disponibles pour l’éducation scolaire et ensuite pour le marché du travail."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f4e7d6dd-2438-41dd-adf9-e5dd179e4c28",
                                                "sense_id": "8f6cdf9d-93fe-30e1-8263-437b6f7482dc",
                                                "text": "Nina, il faut qu'on maintienne la boîte à flot."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8411d9cb-a5ed-4a08-86b6-71cbb01aad6a",
                                                "sense_id": "8f6cdf9d-93fe-30e1-8263-437b6f7482dc",
                                                "text": "Si on veut sauver cet endroit il faut économiser jusqu'à se remettre à flot."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ffcd0dd9-14ea-3b0a-b7ac-3881e32005fc",
                                        "entry_id": "59a9f3ea-b16d-3c44-a4a8-526b8ff66717",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "En l’état."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "figuratively"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e2e29776-5d9e-46ee-9c03-152f1416bb4e",
                                                "sense_id": "ffcd0dd9-14ea-3b0a-b7ac-3881e32005fc",
                                                "text": "Ces efforts pour tenter de maintenir à flot l’accord nucléaire de 2015 interviennent dans un contexte dégradé par la montée des tensions dans le Golfe, où Londres a proposé le déploiement d’une mission navale européenne."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
