            {
                "entry_id": "343a3cad-2561-3d0d-bcf5-8139a5863d6c",
                "word": "afloat",
                "pos": "adv",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "a905e8eb-1770-3088-b0ed-8712e64a35d2",
                        "entry_id": "343a3cad-2561-3d0d-bcf5-8139a5863d6c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "In or into a state of floating."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "not-comparable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "5cb9e2dd-e22d-4ead-a6db-b369e7fc6771",
                                "sense_id": "a905e8eb-1770-3088-b0ed-8712e64a35d2",
                                "text": "You have so little Brains, that a Penn’orth of Butter melted under ’um, would set ’um afloat:"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f1eea40f-6215-4884-826c-a55adf07dd65",
                                "sense_id": "a905e8eb-1770-3088-b0ed-8712e64a35d2",
                                "text": "[…] I went down to my Boat, got the Water out of her, and got her afloat, loaded all my Cargo in her, and then went Home again for more;"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "69fc35f3-63de-4a53-8422-a7029cd1bc6b",
                                "sense_id": "a905e8eb-1770-3088-b0ed-8712e64a35d2",
                                "text": "Oh why is heaven built so far, / Oh why is earth set so remote? / I cannot reach the nearest star / That hangs afloat."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "3127875f-20d4-336c-a262-47c5cd527dda",
                        "entry_id": "343a3cad-2561-3d0d-bcf5-8139a5863d6c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "In, or while in, a vessel at sea or on another body of water; at sea."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "not-comparable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "b7d24ed1-fe3d-4328-af6d-bf56d7c49000",
                                "sense_id": "3127875f-20d4-336c-a262-47c5cd527dda",
                                "text": "[…] that trade […] may likewise employ many useful hands both ashore and afloat,"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2ca2662e-25a1-487f-aafe-92a6b5aece22",
                                "sense_id": "3127875f-20d4-336c-a262-47c5cd527dda",
                                "text": "They was the roughest crew afloat, was Flint’s; the devil himself would have been feared to go to sea with them."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b640a446-85ec-4117-aea4-c37d047be387",
                                "sense_id": "3127875f-20d4-336c-a262-47c5cd527dda",
                                "text": "Navy chow ashore is rarely as good as it is afloat, and for enlisted men it is usually much worse."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "41e2eb12-6979-38c7-8d7c-31bd2a451dca",
                        "entry_id": "343a3cad-2561-3d0d-bcf5-8139a5863d6c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Under water (bearing floating objects)."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "not-comparable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "57098db2-948f-478d-8b27-6335ce14a361",
                                "sense_id": "41e2eb12-6979-38c7-8d7c-31bd2a451dca",
                                "text": "1695, Edmund Gibson (translator), Camden’s Britannia, London: A. Swalle, “Staffordshire,”\n[…] it [the River Dove] overflows and lays the meadows afloat in April, like another Nile."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "3461e77f-2e0c-38cd-a16a-40285dfafc7d",
                        "entry_id": "343a3cad-2561-3d0d-bcf5-8139a5863d6c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "In or into circulation or currency."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "figuratively",
                            "not-comparable",
                            "usually"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "675c8d86-d10f-4cef-b3e2-62f69845a3ef",
                                "sense_id": "3461e77f-2e0c-38cd-a16a-40285dfafc7d",
                                "text": "setting a lie aflote"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "385a0a06-fba9-45b6-a4ec-2d55d030d90b",
                                "sense_id": "3461e77f-2e0c-38cd-a16a-40285dfafc7d",
                                "text": "[…] I shall not be judged fairly; it will get afloat that I am not a good girl,"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "560bed80-5f27-4f35-8a0e-666534dd6613",
                                "sense_id": "3461e77f-2e0c-38cd-a16a-40285dfafc7d",
                                "text": "[…] as this example set the discourse about witchcraft afloat, some people, troubled with a similar complaint, began to fancy themselves bewitched too."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "9ee3c954-8a44-399c-a4b6-b26ebfc65127",
                        "entry_id": "343a3cad-2561-3d0d-bcf5-8139a5863d6c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "In or into a condition of stimulation, arousal, confusion, bewilderment, etc."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "figuratively",
                            "not-comparable",
                            "obsolete"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "19cc93f9-8327-4548-9994-1eafebc0d0e9",
                                "sense_id": "9ee3c954-8a44-399c-a4b6-b26ebfc65127",
                                "text": "No angry passions rise to disturb the silent progress of the work, […] no irritable humours are set afloat:"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8fbd10ee-8941-4cdb-baa2-2a445927cc08",
                                "sense_id": "9ee3c954-8a44-399c-a4b6-b26ebfc65127",
                                "text": "[…] they knew how to abstain from the overdose of liquor that sets the brain afloat and loosens the tongue."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": [
                    {
                        "linkage_id": "bc62834f-a2c0-434f-929b-dd2949633502",
                        "source_entry_id": "343a3cad-2561-3d0d-bcf5-8139a5863d6c",
